From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman V Shaposhnik <rvs@apache.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:26:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] u9fs.c: a read-only, chrooted 9P2000 server for a
 container

- READ_ONLY defaults to 1: only READ_ONLY=0 permits open for
  writing, create, write, remove, wstat or ORCLOSE.
- Plain 9P2000 only: no 9P1 auto-detection, version "9P2000"
  exactly, msize at least 256 and at most -m.
- Frames are bounded: the unsigned length is checked before reading
  into the buffer; short writes are retried.
- Path elements are strict: no empty, ".", "..", "/" or NUL names,
  not even \xx-encoded, and no path longer than PATH_MAX.
- Load the host's passwd and group, then chroot into the export:
  no account lookups happen inside the exported tree.  With -a none,
  -u fixes the user of every attach.
- Serve only regular files and directories, never devices; a
  directory's length is 0 everywhere, as in its qid.
- Tversion clunks all fids; Tremove clunks even on failure; no fid
  may be NOFID.
- Fix leaks (dirread, stat, wstat, create) and a wstat rename in /.
- -l /dev/stderr keeps fd 2, which may not be reopenable.

Co-authored-by: Shelley <shelley@exe.dev>
